1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,592
What does a fee change have to do with card numbers?

2
00:00:02,642 --> 00:00:07,104
Picture your first ticket on a payments team: add a fee to card payments.

3
00:00:07,154 --> 00:00:12,168
You open the code and find card numbers, fees and merchants in one big service.

4
00:00:12,218 --> 00:00:17,520
So a simple fee change touches the card code, and it waits for a card security review.

5
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:20,064
This system splits that service in two.

6
00:00:20,114 --> 00:00:26,136
Each part is a unit: a separate product with its own code, its own install and its own data.

7
00:00:26,186 --> 00:00:28,752
The big unit is ecom, the shop.

8
00:00:28,802 --> 00:00:32,544
The small unit is the cards unit, a locked room next door.

9
00:00:32,594 --> 00:00:34,872
Three kinds of people use the system.

10
00:00:34,922 --> 00:00:37,344
The merchant's server asks for payments.

11
00:00:37,394 --> 00:00:39,432
The buyer pays on the payment page.

12
00:00:39,482 --> 00:00:41,952
And the bank's staff look after the merchants.

13
00:00:42,002 --> 00:00:46,608
ecom is one app built in five parts, and each part is a module.

14
00:00:46,658 --> 00:00:52,608
The modules hold the merchants, the fees, the terminals, the payments, and the checking of the books.

15
00:00:52,658 --> 00:00:56,112
The cards unit is the only place a card number lives.

16
00:00:56,162 --> 00:01:01,968
It is where the buyer types the card, where the number is kept, and where the lines go out to the card networks.

17
00:01:02,018 --> 00:01:06,600
Each unit has its own database, its own keys and its own logins.

18
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:10,440
They share nothing, so nothing in the shop can open the locked room.

19
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:12,312
One line joins them.

20
00:01:12,362 --> 00:01:16,272
ecom calls the cards unit, and the cards unit never calls ecom.

21
00:01:16,322 --> 00:01:20,112
So the cards unit is installed first, and ecom second.

22
00:01:20,162 --> 00:01:21,984
Now back to the ticket.

23
00:01:22,034 --> 00:01:27,504
The fee change lives in the shop alone, in one module, and it never goes near the locked room.

24
00:01:27,554 --> 00:01:30,768
This course builds the locked room first, then the shop.

25
00:01:30,818 --> 00:01:33,072
Now get both units running on your laptop.

26
00:01:33,122 --> 00:01:36,360
Clone the seven repositories into one folder.

27
00:01:36,410 --> 00:01:39,936
Run the cards installer first, then the ecom installer.

28
00:01:39,986 --> 00:01:43,440
Each installer gets its own lesson near the end of the course.

29
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:46,344
Then ask Docker Compose what each unit runs.

30
00:01:46,394 --> 00:01:51,624
The cards unit lists its own Postgres, its own Keycloak and its card services.

31
00:01:51,674 --> 00:01:55,944
ecom lists its own Postgres, its own Keycloak and its own app.

32
00:01:55,994 --> 00:01:59,520
Two lists, two copies of everything, nothing shared.

33
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:02,880
Two units, running: the shop and the locked room.

34
00:02:02,930 --> 00:02:05,208
Next: how a card payment works.
